    "narrative": "**Mickey Moniak** is the clear anchor of today\u2019s lineup with a standout 75.98 efficiency score. The matchup against Gusto is an ideal confluence of variables: a favorable 4.35 xERA, a significant 14% park boost, and an 88% stolen base success rate against the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which aligns perfectly with our organizational mandate to maximize speed. **Josh Naylor** also commands attention at 64.65; while the park factor presents a slight drag, he retains a strong platoon advantage against Ure\u00f1a, and his prime positioning in the #5 hole maximizes his RBI potential. We are monitoring the status of **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland** closely; both carry risks due to pending lineups, but their underlying metrics against V\u00e1squez\u2019s 4.76 xERA remain high enough to justify the start even if they shift down in the order.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Cole Young**, whose 42.77 score kept him in the conversation until the final iteration. Ultimately, the cumulative advantage of the park and platoon profile for **Kyle Karros**\u2014who also benefits from the slow delivery of Gusto\u2014edged out **Cole Young**, who suffers from a regression in the #8 spot against Ure\u00f1a. While **Brice Turang** faces a difficult assignment against the elite arm of Corbin Burnes (3.20 xERA), his prime spot in the #3 order provides enough volume to keep him above our floor. We have benched **Zach McKinstry** and **Edwin Arroyo** strictly due to efficiency thresholds falling below 40.0; we are playing for the highest probability of output today, and with **Trevor Story** still sidelined, we must remain disciplined with our game cap management to ensure we have the flexibility to deploy stars like **Corbin Carroll** or **James Wood** when their individual matchups improve.",
